    {
      "id": "claim_3827ce00321c48dcaad19bfd300ff383",
      "statement": "The TUI configurator is feature-gated behind the optional `tui` Cargo feature, which depends on optional ratatui, crossterm, and ansi-to-tui crates and is enabled by default; `pub mod tui` is gated by `#[cfg(feature = \"tui\")]` in lib.rs, and building with `--no-default-features` yields a minimal render-only hook that never links the TUI dependencies.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Cargo.toml#L18-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c01526f82fe44dba5d0eb38b0d8d68c9ed4adcdb70307b0a8dfde295837be28a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/lib.rs#L48-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7799876f6ba4c732a704ac825a94ac80509b97e8678e637c75c5dffed550f35:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a9dfffb771bf4ae1865b70c0cbaa4d69",
      "statement": "The TUI is never linked on the render hot path: the optional ratatui/crossterm/ansi-to-tui dependencies are only compiled when the `tui` feature is selected, and `render_line`/`render_with` never depend on them.",
